WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.760
A humanoid robot has

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:02.480
to see,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.400
decide and move in

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.080
one continuous loop,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.440
fast enough to work

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.220
beside people.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.320
This is that loop

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.789
on Deepgrid's humanoid platform.

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:15.649
It starts with perception.

00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:17.789
Several sensors are fused

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:19.249
into one three-dimensional

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:21.129
picture of the room,

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:22.689
objects are recognised,

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.149
and depth is measured

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:25.529
in real time,

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:28.481
thirty frames every second.

00:00:28.481 --> 00:00:30.521
Interpretation turns that picture

00:00:30.521 --> 00:00:31.581
into meaning.

00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:33.401
The system reasons about

00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:34.261
context,

00:00:34.261 --> 00:00:36.061
decides what matters,

00:00:36.061 --> 00:00:37.161
and understands a command

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:39.531
spoken in plain language.

00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:41.831
Planning comes next.

00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:43.051
The task is broken

00:00:43.051 --> 00:00:44.151
into steps,

00:00:44.151 --> 00:00:45.631
and each motion is

00:00:45.631 --> 00:00:47.211
planned before a single

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:48.936
joint moves.

00:00:48.936 --> 00:00:50.736
Then action.

00:00:50.736 --> 00:00:52.696
Motor control drives seven

00:00:52.696 --> 00:00:54.396
degrees of freedom with

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:55.936
sub-millimetre precision,

00:00:55.936 --> 00:00:58.916
while motion-control AI keeps

00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:00.716
the robot balanced as

00:01:00.716 --> 00:01:02.036
it walks.

00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.556
An operator can take

00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:04.716
over remotely,

00:01:04.716 --> 00:01:06.176
and the platform keeps

00:01:06.176 --> 00:01:07.616
learning from real-world

00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:08.838
video.

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:09.498
Perception,

00:01:09.498 --> 00:01:10.698
interpretation,

00:01:10.698 --> 00:01:11.278
planning,

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:11.938
action.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.158
One pipeline,

00:01:13.158 --> 00:01:15.638
from silicon to motion.

00:01:15.638 --> 00:01:16.418
What you have seen

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:17.318
is an illustration

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:18.938
of that pipeline,

00:01:18.938 --> 00:01:20.278
not recorded footage.
